Comparison of list-based and generator-based processing based on execution time and memory usage.
# Experiment 04 – List vs Generator

## Aim
Compare list-based processing and generator-based processing for a large dataset in terms of execution time and memory usage.

## Algorithm / Procedure
1. Create a large dataset.
2. Process the dataset using a list.
3. Process the same dataset using a generator.
4. Measure execution time.
5. Compare memory usage.
6. Display the results.

## Program
import time
import sys

n = 100000


# List processing
start = time.time()

list_data = [i * i for i in range(n)]

list_time = time.time() - start


# Generator processing
start = time.time()

generator_data = (i * i for i in range(n))

generator_time = time.time() - start


print("List Processing Time:",
      round(list_time, 6), "seconds")

print("Generator Creation Time:",
      round(generator_time, 6), "seconds")

print("List Memory:",
      sys.getsizeof(list_data), "bytes")

print("Generator Memory:",
      sys.getsizeof(generator_data), "bytes")

## Output
List Processing Time: 0.00845 seconds
Generator Creation Time: 0.000135 seconds
List Memory: 800984 bytes
Generator Memory: 200 bytes

## Observation
Generators use less memory because values are produced one at a time.

## Result
List-based and generator-based processing were successfully compared based on execution time and memory usage.
